headers {
  ~x-paycraft-platform: android
}

docs {
  # PayCraft API — live backend verification

  Runnable against PRODUCTION with the Bruno CLI:

      npx @usebruno/cli run api --env production -r

  ## Why this exists

  Two independent failures this month were invisible to every gate we had, and both were one HTTP
  call away from being obvious:

    * `/config` returned 401 at the Supabase GATEWAY, before the function ran. Every SDK endpoint
      was dead in production while CI smoke reported green, because it accepted 401 as healthy.
    * The dashboard's own login page throws a client-side exception, so the UI cannot be used to
      inspect or fix tenant state at all.

  A file-based collection answers both: it talks to the live backend directly, needs no browser,
  and the assertions live in git next to the code they check.

  ## Secrets

  NO secret is stored here. `environments/production.bru` reads every credential from process env,
  so this directory is safe to commit. Populate them from the vault at call time:

      export PAYCRAFT_ANON_KEY="$(bash ../../../../../core/scripts/secrets-get.sh <alias> --allow-claude-stdout)"

  ...or for interactive use, source a gitignored .env that `/secrets pull` materialises.
}
